# PR review (SE, condensed)

Not QC (`code-quality-gate`) and not SecOps. Engineer loop only.

Author: one intent, <~400 LOC, Conventional Commits, Why/What/How-to-check/Out-of-scope, self-review diff, tests for new behavior.

Reviewer order: intent → fit (BC/ADR) → tests → diff → decision. Timebox 30–45m; else split.

Blockers: wrong behavior, missing tests, invariant/Dependency Rule break, data loss, secrets.
Should: new duplication, swallowed errors, invalid states, missing migration.
Nit: style. Prefix `nit:`.

Comment = what + why + done-looks-like. Suggestion diffs. No sarcasm. No ADR relitigation.

Outcomes: Approve (you would ship) | Request changes (blocker) | Comment only. Re-review the delta.

Author replies: every blocker, "fixed in sha" or "won't + reason". No silent force-push over reviewed commits.

Merge bar: CI green, SE approve, do not impersonate QC/SRE/SecOps.
User sovereignty: propose merge, never click Merge. User decides.
